    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d552-a2">

                <pb facs="0557" n="1291" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1291"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1 in No. 698.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Selfridge to Secretary Herbert.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. S. San Francisco</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Marseilles,
                                France</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November 15,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of an
                    interesting letter from Commander O’Neil, which seems to finish the affair in
                    Adana.</p>
                <p>I have directed the <hi rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi> to proceed to Jaffa,
                    and then to meet this ship at Alexandretta, December 5, 1895, visiting the
                    several intermediate points where there are missionaries or American
                    interests.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thos. O. Selfridge</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S. N.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
